---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = '2026-09-29';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy - Crontinel"
  description="Crontinel privacy policy. What data we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and the rights you have over your personal information."
>
<script type="application/ld+json" slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://crontinel.com" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Privacy Policy", "item": "https://crontinel.com/legal/privacy/" }
  ]
}
</script>

  <Nav />

  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 prose prose-invert prose-gray max-w-none" id="main-content">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-10">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Who we are</h2>
        <p>Crontinel is operated by Harun R Rayhan. The service is available at crontinel.com and app.crontinel.com. Contact: <a href="mailto:support@crontinel.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white">support@crontinel.com</a></p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Account data:</strong> email address, name, password hash (bcrypt)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Monitoring data:</strong> cron runs, queue and Horizon status, monitor settings, and any command output your app sends to Crontinel</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Billing data:</strong> subscription status. Payment details are handled directly by Stripe; we never see your card number</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Service logs:</strong> request and diagnostic data, which can include IP addresses</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Hosted AI:</strong> if you turn on AI investigations, selected monitoring evidence is sent to Cloudflare Workers AI to generate an analysis</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Analytics:</strong> page views and clicks on crontinel.com via Google Analytics 4, only if you consent via the cookie banner</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>We do not use advertising or tracking cookies on app.crontinel.com</li>
          <li>We do not sell your data to any third party</li>
          <li>We do not access the content of your queued jobs or cron command output unless you explicitly send it to us</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Cookies</h2>
        <p>We use two categories of cookies:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Strictly necessary:</strong> session cookie, CSRF token. No consent required.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Analytics:</strong> Google Analytics 4 on crontinel.com only. Only set after you click "Accept" on the cookie banner.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Data retention</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>Cron runs, monitor events, and resolved alerts are pruned under the applicable plan's 7, 30, 90, or 365-day history limit. Open alerts can remain while the issue is active.</li>
          <li>When an organization closes, its configuration and invitations become eligible for cleanup after 30 days, once billing closure is verified. A hold can delay cleanup.</li>
          <li>Audit and billing records, monitoring history, and database backups can remain after account closure. Their separate retention periods have not been finalized. Contact us about a specific deletion request.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Your rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>If you are in the EU/EEA, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Access</strong> the data we hold about you</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Export</strong> your profile, organization, app, and monitor settings as JSON from your profile settings</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Request deletion</strong> through your profile settings or by contacting us. Owner deletion closes the organization and its billing when billing can be reconciled; it does not immediately erase all records.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Object</strong> to processing: contact us at support@crontinel.com</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Data location</h2>
        <p>Crontinel uses Railway for the application and database, and Cloudflare for site delivery and optional hosted AI. These services can process data outside the EU/EEA. We do not offer an EU-only processing commitment.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Third-party services</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Stripe</strong>, payment processing. Subject to Stripe's privacy policy.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Resend</strong>, transactional email delivery.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Railway</strong>, application and database hosting.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Cloudflare</strong>, site delivery and optional Workers AI investigations.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-300">Google Analytics</strong>, landing page analytics, consent-gated.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-base mb-2">Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions? <a href="mailto:support@crontinel.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white">support@crontinel.com</a></p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
